               <value>
                  <exData contentType="text/html">
                     <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-size:13pt;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">INSTRUCTIONS:<span style="font-size:10pt;text-decoration:none"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">  </span></span><span style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none">Please attach a legible copy of your DD214 to document your status as a veteran of the United States Armed Forces.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><span style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none">Incomplete documents will not be returned. They will be disposed of in a secure manner, per university policy. This will delay processing.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span></p><p style="font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">A “veteran” is defined as one of the following:<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="margin-bottom:5pt;font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">1)<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">         </span>Someone who has engaged in active duty in the Army, Navy, Air Force, Marines, or Coast Guard.</p><p style="margin-bottom:5pt;font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">2)<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">         </span>A member of the National Guard or Reserves who was called to active duty for purposes other than training.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">3)<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">         </span>A cadet or midshipman at one of the service academies and was released under a condition, other than</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">            </span>dishonorable.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0in">If you cannot provide the documentation, because you are<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="text-decoration:underline">not</span> a veteran, check this box<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">         </span>and sign the certification below.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></p></body>
                  </exData>
               </value>
